From: lu5je0 <lu5je0@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/udev: keep matching backlights while the display is off

The DRM connector's enabled attribute describes its current scanout state,
not whether a backlight belongs to it. DPMS off makes it "disabled".
Reconfiguring monitors in that state drops the backlight, and DPMS on does
not recreate it, leaving GNOME's native brightness control unavailable.

Match by the raw backlight's DRM connector parent and connector name even
while scanout is disabled. Monitor activity is tracked separately by the
monitor manager.

--- a/src/backends/meta-udev.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-udev.c
@@ -282,10 +282,10 @@ meta_udev_backlight_find_for_connector (GList      *devices,
       if (!prop || !g_str_has_suffix (prop, connector_suffix))
         continue;
 
-      /* Also make sure the connector is actually enabled */
-      prop = g_udev_device_get_sysfs_attr (parent, "enabled");
-      if (g_strcmp0 (prop, "enabled") != 0)
-        continue;
+      /* DPMS off disables scanout, but does not change which connector owns
+       * this backlight. Keep it available across monitor reconfiguration
+       * while the display is off.
+       */
 
       return g_object_ref (device);
     }
